{"task":"transcribe","language":"english","duration":41.720001220703125,"text":"This is the statue the museums began with, a bearded man and two boys struggle with two enormous snakes coiled around them. He is Lauecorn, a priest of Troy, who warned the Trojans not to bring the wooden horse into the city. The gods who wanted Troy to fall sent the snakes out of the sea. The marble is a little over two meters tall, and the Roman writer Pliny says three sculptors from Rhodes carved it. It was found in 1506 in a vineyard. Lauecorn's right arm was missing. It turned up by chance in 1905, bent exactly as Michelangelo had guessed 400 years earlier, and was put back in 1957.","words":[{"word":"This","start":0,"end":0.6200000047683716},{"word":"is","start":0.6200000047683716,"end":0.8600000143051147},{"word":"the","start":0.8600000143051147,"end":1.2599999904632568},{"word":"statue","start":1.2599999904632568,"end":1.4600000381469727},{"word":"the","start":1.4600000381469727,"end":1.8600000143051147},{"word":"museums","start":1.8600000143051147,"end":2.2200000286102295},{"word":"began","start":2.2200000286102295,"end":2.640000104904175},{"word":"with","start":2.640000104904175,"end":3},{"word":"a","start":3.059999942779541,"end":3.7200000286102295},{"word":"bearded","start":3.7200000286102295,"end":4.139999866485596},{"word":"man","start":4.139999866485596,"end":4.400000095367432},{"word":"and","start":4.400000095367432,"end":4.71999979019165},{"word":"two","start":4.71999979019165,"end":5},{"word":"boys","start":5,"end":5.420000076293945},{"word":"struggle","start":5.420000076293945,"end":5.880000114440918},{"word":"with","start":5.880000114440918,"end":6.21999979019165},{"word":"two","start":6.21999979019165,"end":6.860000133514404},{"word":"enormous","start":6.860000133514404,"end":7.300000190734863},{"word":"snakes","start":7.300000190734863,"end":7.760000228881836},{"word":"coiled","start":7.760000228881836,"end":8.119999885559082},{"word":"around","start":8.119999885559